  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><msub><mi>Fe</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>OH</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>OAc</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mi>Cl</mi></math>&nbsp;is a coordination complex containing iron ions coordinated with hydroxide and acetate&nbsp;ligands. When dissolved in water, this complex can undergo hydrolysis and dissociation.&nbsp;</p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><msub><mi>Fe</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>OH</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>OAc</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mi>Cl</mi></math> dissolves in water. Rest of the complexes form precipitate.</p>",
    "image": null
